;
; demand_mutual_content_1 -- mutual-recursion-in-a-demanded-body witness
; (test-matrix C12; the stage-d E2 referee hole). A bound #query `reach`
; over `ra`, whose body is a two-view SCC: `ra` and `rb` are mutually
; recursive through `step` (ra <- rb <- ra). Distinct in shape from
; demand_recursive_content_1 (a NON-recursive wrapper over a single
; self-recursive relation) and demand_cyclic_1 (a query directly on the
; recursive relation): here the demanded relation's OWN body sits in a
; multi-view recursive SCC. Under -demand (.drflags = `-demand`) the reject
; fires in the DataFlow demand body-walk ("Unsupported rule-body shape under
; -demand") -- the shadowed recursive-content belt (R-BODYWALK) -- in ALL
; FOUR optimization modes. The .main.cpp is inert / never compiled.
;
; The .batches + oracle goldens pin the DEFINITIONAL mutual-fixpoint answer
; NOW, BEFORE the Stage-D lift that will let this compile: the oracle runs
; the plain (undemanded) program and is the ONLY pre-lift referee for the
; even/odd step-parity split (ra = even-step reachable from base, rb = odd).

#message base(u64 K, u64 V).
#message step(u64 V, u64 W).
#local ra(u64 K, u64 V).
#local rb(u64 K, u64 V).
ra(K, V) : base(K, V).
ra(K, W) : rb(K, V), step(V, W).
rb(K, W) : ra(K, V), step(V, W).
#query reach(bound u64 K, free u64 V) : ra(K, V).
